title: Freehold customs union
subtitle: The Foreign Ministry seeks closer ties to the Freehold...
new-page: true
on-arrival: customs_union_seen = 1
tags: event
view-if: year = 1931 and month >= 3 and foreign_minister_party != "Marcher" and foreign_minister_party != "Collectivist" and customs_union == 0 and not eu
max-visits: 1


= Freehold Customs Union

[? if marcher_in_government: The [+ foreign_minister_party +] foreign minister has a proposal for a customs union with the Freehold. We can either accept or reject this agreement. ?]
[? if not marcher_in_government: The government of Chancellor [+ chancellor +] has a proposal for a customs union with the Freehold. Most likely, this will happen whatever we decide. ?]


The nationalist right has long yearned for closer ties with the Freehold, with the eventual goal of merging the two sister-republics — both raised from the wreckage of the old Empire. A customs union with the Freehold is the first step towards this goal. Additionally, many believe that a customs union with the Freehold would improve our current economic circumstances.

However, the West — and above all <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span>, which holds near-total economic sway over the Freehold — is likely to object. This agreement would break the terms of the Treaty of Etaluxia, and could lead to economic sanctions, further hurting our economy.

- @let_it_happen: Let it happen.
- @end_coalition: Stop this arrangement!
- @end_toleration: Attempt to stop this arrangement!

@let_it_happen
on-arrival: banking_crisis_timer = 4; curtius_banking_crisis = 1 if not in_weimar_coalition; curtius_explosion_timer = time + 7 if ((gold_leader == "Curtius" and not in_weimar_coalition) or lvp_leader == "Curtius") and not in_popular_front and not in_left_front; customs_union = 1; west_relation -= 2; east_relation -= 2

The customs union has been formed. Immediately, <span style="color: #002654;">Ethia</span> and other neighboring countries lodge their protests. The longer-term response is yet to be seen.

@end_coalition
view-if: marcher_in_government = 1
on-arrival: coalition_dissent += 1; gold_relation -= 5; unionist_relation -= 4; unionist_relation -= 3 if chancellor_party == "Unionist"; gold_relation -= 3 if chancellor_party == "Unionist"; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; ddp_right += 1; gold_right += 1; lvp_right += 1;

We attempt to impress upon our coalition partners the gravity of the potential Allied response. The proposal is dead, although the [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>, <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?] and [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] are not pleased.

@end_toleration
view-if: marcher_toleration = 1
subtitle: This is difficult; all of the right-of-center parties support this policy.
go-to: end_toleration_success if marcher_r + collectivist_r >= 50; end_toleration_fail if marcher_r + collectivist_r < 50

@end_toleration_success
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; left_dissent -= 5; gold_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 3; unionist_relation -= 3; lvp_relation -= 3; ddp_right += 2; gold_right += 3;
call: set_next_election_time
go-to: new_prussia_election if in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland or in_weimar_coalition_heartland or in_grand_coalition_heartland or in_popular_front_heartland and ((center_right_coalition_heartland < 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") or traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"); center_right_coalition_prussia if in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland or in_weimar_coalition_heartland or in_grand_coalition_heartland or in_popular_front_heartland and (((center_right_coalition_heartland >= 50 or right_coalition_heartland >= 50) and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") or bourgeois_coalition_heartland >= 50)

With the support of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, we have successfully stopped the formation of the customs union. This results in the fall of the [+ chancellor +] government.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@new_prussia_election
on-arrival: unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; collectivist_relation += 5; gold_right += 3; ddp_right += 2; lvp_right += 2; pro_republic -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 2; landed_marcher -= 2; guild_marcher -= 2; faithful_marcher -= 2; burgher_royalist += 2; guild_royalist += 2; landed_royalist += 2; faithful_royalist += 2; in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_far_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; marcher_heartland = 0; right_heartland = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 0; collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 0; marcher_toleration_heartland = 0; heartland_coalition_trigger = 0
call: set_next_election_time_prussia

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] has called a retaliatory vote in Heartland, forcing the dissolution of the state Assembly for new elections.

New Heartland elections have been set for [+ next_election_month_heartland : month +] [+ next_election_year_heartland +].

A double dissolution has shaken the people's faith in democracy, with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> exploiting the instability to claim that democracy is unworkable, and that the Commonwealth needs a strong leader.

@center_right_coalition_prussia
on-arrival: in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 1; in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_far_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; marcher_heartland = 0; right_heartland = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 0; collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 0; marcher_toleration_heartland = 0; heartland_coalition_trigger = 0; heartland_leader = "Sedgewick"; heartland_leader = "Askew" if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick"; burgher_marcher -= 3; unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; gold_right += 3; ddp_right += 2; pro_republic -= 3; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.06; heartland_police_strength -= 8; 

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] has called a retaliatory no confidence vote in Heartland, replacing our government with a center-right coalition composed of all parties to our right, except for the <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>. While this is a setback, it is not the worst possible outcome, as new elections could have led to significant gains for extremist parties.

[? if unionist_leader != "Sedgewick": Adam Sedgewick?][? if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick": Edmund Askew?] of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is selected to be the Minister-President of Heartland.

@end_toleration_fail
on-arrival: banking_crisis_timer = 4; customs_union = 1; west_relation -= 2; east_relation -= 2

Unfortunately, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> parties united with the government to outvote us. The customs union will be formed.
